A comment opened above a procedure whose first `;` is inside the
procedure's code. The comment ends there (no comment_termination), and
the code that remains reads as fragments. Records the downstream damage:
the :PROCEDURE line is swallowed, so its :ENDPROC is unmatched
(diag.comment_termination "Note", diag.unmatched_block_end).
-- input.ssl --
/* Helper: trims and upper-cases a code
:PROCEDURE CleanCode;
	:PARAMETERS sCode;
	:RETURN Upper(AllTrim(sCode));
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
/* Helper: trims and upper-cases a code
:PROCEDURE CleanCode;
:PARAMETERS sCode;
:RETURN Upper(AllTrim(sCode));
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
5:1-5:9 error unmatched_block_end: Unexpected ':ENDPROC' without matching block start
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
5:1-5:9 error unmatched_block_end: Unexpected ':ENDPROC' without matching block start
